1
00:01:05,042 --> 00:01:07,172
911. What's your emergency?

2
00:01:08,132 --> 00:01:09,292
Hello?

3
00:01:11,463 --> 00:01:13,423
This is 911. Go ahead.

4
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:18,042
This is Suh Young-chul, who used to work at Chains Bio.

5
00:01:18,882 --> 00:01:23,172
Today at the Doongwoori Building I plan to run an experiment.

6
00:01:23,543 --> 00:01:26,252
Excuse me? Can you repeat that, please?

7
00:01:26,292 --> 00:01:28,583
Ah, not an experiment.

8
00:01:28,882 --> 00:01:30,292
It's closer to terrorism.

9
00:01:30,463 --> 00:01:31,293
What?

10
00:01:31,423 --> 00:01:36,293
That's right. A highly contagious bioterror attack.

11
00:01:39,962 --> 00:01:42,792
I tested the pathogen in my body.

12
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:51,293
And it was a success.

13
00:01:52,713 --> 00:01:56,832
I am the only vaccine that can stop this outbreak.

14
00:02:00,293 --> 00:02:02,293
Organisms of the same species that,

15
00:02:02,333 --> 00:02:04,543
for a certain time, live in the same place

16
00:02:18,832 --> 00:02:20,423
Why are you waiting for me?

17
00:02:21,882 --> 00:02:24,583
You're 10 minutes late. What was it this time?

18
00:02:25,583 --> 00:02:26,882
It was nothing.

19
00:02:27,002 --> 00:02:27,752
Traffic was bad,

20
00:02:27,832 --> 00:02:30,172
so the taxi driver tried to let me off across the street.

21
00:02:30,633 --> 00:02:30,962
So ?

22
00:02:32,212 --> 00:02:34,333
Yeah, these things happen.

23
00:02:35,212 --> 00:02:38,463
It's okay if I say it, but how can he say that to me?

24
00:02:38,503 --> 00:02:39,583
So ?

25
00:02:41,713 --> 00:02:43,132
It's not what I wanted.

26
00:02:43,383 --> 00:02:45,082
I said, however long it takes,

27
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:47,002
drop me off at the spot I chose.

28
00:02:51,583 --> 00:02:52,543
What?

29
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:55,172
So it's my fault again?

30
00:02:55,423 --> 00:02:57,543
Welcome to the Chains Blo Conference,

31
00:02:57,543 --> 00:02:59,962
a leading platform for future technology.

32
00:03:00,002 --> 00:03:01,042
Thank you.

33
00:03:01,503 --> 00:03:03,423
You brought the invitation I gave you?

34
00:03:03,882 --> 00:03:06,832
...and now we'll hear from CEO Kang Woo-cheol.

35
00:03:06,882 --> 00:03:08,713
Please give him a round of applause.

36
00:03:14,792 --> 00:03:15,673
Is that the guy?

37
00:03:15,673 --> 00:03:18,293
The one I should grovel to if I want to work here?

38
00:03:19,463 --> 00:03:22,082
If only you got along with your dean,

39
00:03:22,082 --> 00:03:24,082
this wouldn't be necessary.

40
00:03:25,042 --> 00:03:27,463
Sure, my fault again.

41
00:03:28,383 --> 00:03:30,132
But don't you care how that dean

42
00:03:30,132 --> 00:03:31,792
treated his graduate students?

43
00:03:31,792 --> 00:03:33,213
No, I don't.

44
00:03:33,633 --> 00:03:36,082
Well, I'm sure he's a jerk.

45
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:38,213
And you couldn't tolerate that.

46
00:03:38,882 --> 00:03:41,293
So you got on his bad side, and didn't get reappointed.

47
00:03:44,132 --> 00:03:46,132
I'm just curious...

48
00:03:46,633 --> 00:03:48,922
Why are you so fixated on your ex-wife's career

49
00:03:48,922 --> 00:03:50,293
10 years after the divorce?

50
00:03:52,082 --> 00:03:53,752
Because you have no friends.

51
00:03:54,503 --> 00:03:57,383
You keep doing things that make people hate you.

52
00:03:57,383 --> 00:03:59,832
Does your wife know you look after your ex-wife like this?

53
00:03:59,832 --> 00:04:03,383
My wife is not as sensitive as you are.

54
00:04:03,882 --> 00:04:05,962
She's probably even concerned for you.

55
00:04:06,673 --> 00:04:07,922
What a cool wife.

56
00:04:08,503 --> 00:04:11,253
You're a great match. I'm happy for you.

57
00:04:11,423 --> 00:04:14,002
If I say our company's main business

58
00:04:14,002 --> 00:04:16,002
is collective intelligence,

59
00:04:16,002 --> 00:04:17,503
people might wonder,

60
00:04:17,633 --> 00:04:19,042
"Why is a bio company,

61
00:04:19,042 --> 00:04:22,213
rather than an IT company, studying that topic?"

62
00:04:22,713 --> 00:04:25,383
Collective intelligence is a common term

63
00:04:25,383 --> 00:04:27,213
in the field of sociology,

64
00:04:27,383 --> 00:04:30,383
but the first person to use the term

65
00:04:30,543 --> 00:04:33,383
was an entomologist who studied ants,

66
00:04:33,423 --> 00:04:35,253
William Morton Wheeler.

67
00:04:35,543 --> 00:04:38,792
Collective intelligence is a key force driving evolution.

68
00:04:39,133 --> 00:04:42,293
You know the yellow slime mold 'Physarum polycephalum'?

69
00:04:42,713 --> 00:04:44,383
These fellows upgrade themselves

70
00:04:44,383 --> 00:04:45,882
through information exchange

71
00:04:45,882 --> 00:04:49,082
and optimize the direction of their growth towards food.

72
00:04:49,583 --> 00:04:51,583
Although not multicellular organisms,

73
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:53,173
they can learn and remember.

74
00:04:53,633 --> 00:04:56,173
Inspired by these remarkable traits,

75
00:04:56,173 --> 00:04:57,922
we were able to dramatically improve

76
00:04:57,962 --> 00:05:00,002
the production of organic semiconductors.

77
00:05:00,423 --> 00:05:03,002
Let's give a hand to our little collaborators.

78
00:05:07,042 --> 00:05:09,543
This guy's more interesting than I expected.

79
00:05:09,792 --> 00:05:12,633
This isn't some lame company that makes copycat drugs.

80
00:05:12,752 --> 00:05:14,752
It's a serious, enterprising firm.

81
00:05:15,083 --> 00:05:16,583
After I introduced you,

82
00:05:16,583 --> 00:05:18,792
they even sent another invitation for you.

83
00:05:19,792 --> 00:05:21,922
Actually, that's why I came.

84
00:05:22,503 --> 00:05:25,213
I was curious what this message meant.

85
00:05:25,383 --> 00:05:27,293
To Prof. Kwon: Imperfect communication,

86
00:05:27,333 --> 00:05:28,583
the source of all tragedy

87
00:05:28,633 --> 00:05:31,922
...so this chip helps damaged nerves carry information.

88
00:05:32,083 --> 00:05:35,673
We injected it into a rat with severed spinal nerves

89
00:05:35,713 --> 00:05:37,463
and paralyzed hind legs,

90
00:05:38,042 --> 00:05:41,253
and as you can see, just a moment later,

91
00:05:41,713 --> 00:05:44,882
It was able to move no different from a healthy rat.

92
00:05:52,133 --> 00:05:54,133
If we continue with this research,

93
00:05:54,133 --> 00:05:56,463
and apply it to the human brain,

94
00:05:56,673 --> 00:05:59,792
I believe it may enable a direct transfer

95
00:05:59,832 --> 00:06:02,583
of information between individuals.

96
00:06:03,673 --> 00:06:05,002
When that happens,

97
00:06:05,383 --> 00:06:07,173
we may live in a world where

98
00:06:07,213 --> 00:06:10,383
you can't think bad thoughts in front of others.

99
00:06:11,922 --> 00:06:13,792
Thank you, CEO Kang.

100
00:06:13,962 --> 00:06:16,423
Please give him a round of applause!

101
00:06:23,962 --> 00:06:26,383
Next, to introduce Chains Bio's global market strategy...

102
00:06:33,713 --> 00:06:35,673
It's your first vacation in ages.

103
00:06:36,003 --> 00:06:39,543
So why spend it with the younger brother you see every day?

104
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:43,882
This way I can get some fresh air, go shopping...

105
00:06:43,882 --> 00:06:46,293
You know how stifling it is working at a computer all day?

106
00:06:51,293 --> 00:06:54,922
Wow, look at all the camping stuff they have these days.

107
00:06:55,133 --> 00:06:56,713
I could just live outdoors.

108
00:06:57,962 --> 00:06:59,423
The clothes are nice, too.

109
00:07:01,423 --> 00:07:03,713
Should we go camping? On your next vacation?

110
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:06,792
-The two of us? - Yeah, let's go.

111
00:07:07,083 --> 00:07:08,423
We'll grill some meat...

112
00:07:08,503 --> 00:07:10,173
That'd be great!

113
00:07:10,673 --> 00:07:12,293
We can go, why not?

114
00:07:12,293 --> 00:07:14,882
That's great. I'll buy some equipment. SECURITY

115
00:07:15,633 --> 00:07:18,003
You get back to work. Lunchtime will end soon.

116
00:07:18,003 --> 00:07:20,832
- No, I'll head back after you. - No need.

117
00:07:20,832 --> 00:07:23,543
The facilities here are great. So convenient.

118
00:07:24,253 --> 00:07:28,713
Don't I work my ass off so I can live in civilization?

119
00:07:28,713 --> 00:07:30,963
You always go on about civilization,

120
00:07:30,963 --> 00:07:32,882
why do you want to go camping?

121
00:07:32,882 --> 00:07:34,543
Camping is civilization, too.

122
00:07:34,752 --> 00:07:36,673
Go on. See you at home.

123
00:07:36,963 --> 00:07:38,503
I'll look around before going.

124
00:07:39,922 --> 00:07:40,543
Selamat tinggal.

125
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:40,752
-Take care..- Yeah.

126
00:07:42,043 --> 00:07:42,293
Take care. Yeah.

127
00:07:46,003 --> 00:07:48,792
Hello, sir. I enjoyed your presentation.

128
00:07:48,923 --> 00:07:50,503
Oh, Professor Han.

129
00:07:50,713 --> 00:07:54,083
This is Professor Kwon Se-jeong, who I mentioned last time.

130
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:55,882
Thank you for inviting me.

131
00:07:55,923 --> 00:07:58,503
And for this note on my invitation.

132
00:07:59,463 --> 00:08:00,713
Just a moment.

133
00:08:01,583 --> 00:08:02,633
Hello?

134
00:08:02,792 --> 00:08:03,882
Mr. Kang Woo-cheol?

135
00:08:04,383 --> 00:08:06,133
Yes. Who's speaking?

136
00:08:06,173 --> 00:08:08,923
I'm Lee Bong-seok, from the Seoul Counterterrorism Squad.

137
00:08:09,043 --> 00:08:10,333
How can I help you?

138
00:08:10,503 --> 00:08:12,213
You know a man named Suh Young-chul?

139
00:08:12,963 --> 00:08:15,633
This call seems important. Let's talk later.

140
00:08:15,633 --> 00:08:17,713
Ah, sure. We'll wait.

141
00:08:21,253 --> 00:08:23,383
You sure he's the one who sent this invitation?

142
00:08:23,423 --> 00:08:25,213
What are you doing? Go after him.

143
00:08:25,423 --> 00:08:25,923
What?

144
00:08:25,923 --> 00:08:27,713
Just hand him your card

145
00:08:27,752 --> 00:08:31,003
and say "I'm Kwon Se-jeong," that's all. ,

146
00:08:39,253 --> 00:08:41,463
Why are you looking for Dr. Suh?

147
00:08:41,713 --> 00:08:42,713
We received a call

148
00:08:42,713 --> 00:08:45,003
that Dr. Suh is planning a terrorist attack

149
00:08:45,003 --> 00:08:47,213
in the building hosting your conference.

150
00:08:49,883 --> 00:08:51,883
I think I saw him today at the conference.

151
00:08:52,043 --> 00:08:53,043
Are you certain?

152
00:08:53,752 --> 00:08:55,133
Not 100% certain.

153
00:08:55,383 --> 00:08:56,883
He was standing too far away.

154
00:08:57,083 --> 00:08:59,463
Our team will arrive there soon.

155
00:08:59,463 --> 00:09:01,713
If you see him again, call me immediately at this number.

156
00:09:01,713 --> 00:09:03,083
All right, I will.

157
00:09:28,833 --> 00:09:30,503
Nice speech, Woo-cheol.

158
00:09:30,923 --> 00:09:32,213
So impressive.

159
00:09:33,083 --> 00:09:35,213
Information exchange through organic semiconductors?

160
00:09:36,043 --> 00:09:39,963
You know how hard I researched that.

161
00:09:41,083 --> 00:09:43,463
Consciousness in a multilateral network.

162
00:09:44,043 --> 00:09:46,883
Well, if that existed,

163
00:09:47,463 --> 00:09:50,503
no one would be betrayed and kicked out like me, right?

164
00:09:50,963 --> 00:09:52,213
You freak.

165
00:09:53,583 --> 00:09:56,923
The technology you researched can't be used anywhere.

166
00:09:58,423 --> 00:09:59,253
Bro.

167
00:10:00,043 --> 00:10:03,333
I'm taking humanity to the next level.

168
00:10:04,793 --> 00:10:07,293
Enabling a second cognitive revolution.

169
00:10:12,503 --> 00:10:13,673
You know what?

170
00:10:14,213 --> 00:10:15,383
You...

171
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:18,333
are just a psycho.

172
00:10:18,883 --> 00:10:20,963
Get lost, you loser!

173
00:10:26,043 --> 00:10:27,833
But when you hired me,

174
00:10:28,293 --> 00:10:30,673
you said my research was great.

175
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:32,923
That you respected my research.

176
00:10:33,963 --> 00:10:38,043
It was all just an act, so you could steal my research.

177
00:10:39,043 --> 00:10:40,793
And now... psycho?

178
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:43,963
You stole research from that psycho.

179
00:10:45,333 --> 00:10:49,253
You just want to make humans go extinct, don't you?

180
00:10:50,213 --> 00:10:51,883
Not extinct.

181
00:10:52,003 --> 00:10:53,333
It's a birth.

182
00:10:53,753 --> 00:10:55,333
The birth of a new humanity.

183
00:10:55,753 --> 00:10:57,293
Just imagine it.

184
00:10:57,503 --> 00:10:59,963
Perfect communication will be possible.

185
00:11:00,253 --> 00:11:02,793
All the byproducts of crass individualism,

186
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:04,793
jealousy, rivalry, suspicion...

187
00:11:06,463 --> 00:11:10,003
Those bizarre losses that arise from unstable communication.

188
00:11:10,333 --> 00:11:12,213
That's what I'm trying to stop.

189
00:11:15,714 --> 00:11:16,753
Wow!

190
00:11:20,083 --> 00:11:22,133
You crazy freak.

191
00:11:23,883 --> 00:11:24,963
Give it a try.

192
00:11:25,253 --> 00:11:26,673
It's got nothing to do with me.

193
00:11:27,083 --> 00:11:29,753
I'm clocking out, so good luck with that.

194
00:11:31,543 --> 00:11:35,923
I want you to be the link between me and the new humanity.

195
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:43,923
What the hell are you doing?

196
00:11:44,253 --> 00:11:45,213
Research.

197
00:11:45,253 --> 00:11:46,583
You goddamned maniac!

198
00:12:28,503 --> 00:12:29,714
Hey, look at this.

199
00:12:30,173 --> 00:12:31,213
Hey mister!

200
00:12:31,293 --> 00:12:32,793
Shouldn't we call 911?

201
00:12:51,963 --> 00:12:52,963
Did you talk to him?

202
00:12:55,583 --> 00:12:56,923
Seemed like a bad time.

203
00:12:56,923 --> 00:12:58,923
Really? Just a sec.

204
00:13:01,003 --> 00:13:03,753
No, really. I don't think he'll want to talk now.

205
00:13:10,293 --> 00:13:12,753
Let's go eat. He'll call back.

206
00:13:25,383 --> 00:13:27,543
Police. Where's the conference hall?

207
00:13:27,674 --> 00:13:30,173
Turn left and go up the stairs, then...

208
00:13:35,173 --> 00:13:36,133
What is that?

209
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:40,963
Go.

210
00:13:42,173 --> 00:13:43,674
Sir, are you okay?

211
00:13:49,753 --> 00:13:51,133
Call the containment team. - What?

212
00:13:51,133 --> 00:13:52,463
Call for a lockdown!

213
00:14:01,463 --> 00:14:02,133
Hi!

214
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:04,634
Where are you, Daddy? What are you doing?

215
00:14:04,793 --> 00:14:06,463
I'll head home now.

216
00:14:06,584 --> 00:14:08,923
Honey, where's your passport?

217
00:14:09,043 --> 00:14:11,293
Should be in the drawer in the study.

218
00:14:12,423 --> 00:14:14,963
- You still with Professor Kwon? - Yeah.

219
00:14:14,963 --> 00:14:16,423
I'll head home soon.

220
00:14:16,923 --> 00:14:17,923
Want to say hi?

221
00:14:21,463 --> 00:14:23,383
Anyway, hurry home. We need to pack.

222
00:14:23,544 --> 00:14:24,253
Okay.

223
00:14:24,253 --> 00:14:26,883
Say bye to Dad. - Hurry home, Dad!

224
00:14:28,293 --> 00:14:29,793
Where are you going? Traveling?

225
00:14:33,883 --> 00:14:36,544
Why don't you answer? You immigrating or something?

226
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:38,463
Well...

227
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:41,544
A teaching position opened at UC Irvine...

228
00:14:41,793 --> 00:14:44,833
Really, you're going to the US? For how long?

229
00:14:45,584 --> 00:14:48,213
This time, we may just stay there.

230
00:14:55,173 --> 00:14:57,793
Ah, now I get it.

231
00:14:58,423 --> 00:15:00,463
You're leaving, so you wanted to set

232
00:15:00,504 --> 00:15:02,833
your ex-wife up with a job before going?

233
00:15:03,793 --> 00:15:05,043
Anyway, congrats.

234
00:15:05,173 --> 00:15:06,793
It's good news, right?

235
00:15:10,043 --> 00:15:12,463
Since it's the last time, let me ask.

236
00:15:13,753 --> 00:15:15,714
Why did you marry me?

237
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:20,883
Well...

238
00:15:21,753 --> 00:15:25,293
The way you never back down when you think you're right...

239
00:15:25,293 --> 00:15:26,923
your personality?

240
00:15:27,083 --> 00:15:30,634
Wow, after you always begged me not to do that.

241
00:15:30,883 --> 00:15:32,253
You liked that?

242
00:15:33,674 --> 00:15:36,464
I did... I liked it.

243
00:15:37,464 --> 00:15:39,213
But I couldn't keep up with you.

244
00:15:39,584 --> 00:15:41,634
I couldn't handle it.

245
00:15:42,083 --> 00:15:44,833
I've always been a bit of a coward.

246
00:15:46,253 --> 00:15:48,464
That's why I broke up with you.

247
00:15:52,133 --> 00:15:54,833
Don't worry. I'll be okay.

248
00:15:55,963 --> 00:15:58,584
It's not like you, talking like that.

249
00:15:59,634 --> 00:16:00,963
I'm not saying you should change...

250
00:16:00,963 --> 00:16:02,043
Done eating?

251
00:16:02,383 --> 00:16:04,833
Let's go, your wife is waiting.

252
00:16:05,634 --> 00:16:07,293
There she goes again....

253
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:12,833
Thank you.

254
00:16:14,634 --> 00:16:16,253
Have a good evening.

255
00:16:18,003 --> 00:16:19,253
Welcome.

256
00:16:19,464 --> 00:16:21,213
Shit, that's so funny. Yeah...

257
00:16:22,634 --> 00:16:24,173
Hey, I'll call you back.

258
00:16:24,383 --> 00:16:26,083
I'm gonna stuff my face.

259
00:16:26,504 --> 00:16:27,173
Yeah.

260
00:16:29,753 --> 00:16:31,544
Three people? - Yes, three.

261
00:16:31,714 --> 00:16:35,504
From here to here....we'll take it all.

262
00:16:36,003 --> 00:16:36,634
All of it?

263
00:16:37,003 --> 00:16:38,213
Yeah, all of it.

264
00:16:43,504 --> 00:16:45,504
You're paying today.

265
00:16:46,544 --> 00:16:47,173
Faham Got it?

266
00:16:50,753 --> 00:16:52,674
Damn it, So-eun!

267
00:16:53,504 --> 00:16:55,714
You should answer him, huh?

268
00:16:59,963 --> 00:17:02,083
The entire building is being locked down.

269
00:17:02,253 --> 00:17:04,963
Security personnel, evacuate everyone immediately!

270
00:17:06,293 --> 00:17:07,003
What's going on?

271
00:17:10,833 --> 00:17:11,714
Hey!

272
00:17:20,043 --> 00:17:20,833
Everyone evacuate!

273
00:17:20,883 --> 00:17:22,544
Move! Out of the way!

274
